The key insight here is that this function only exists in chain mode—ring mode operations don't have an init function at all. So for SG2002, which uses DWMAC1000, the initialization path depends on whether chain_mode is set in the module parameters. If it is, the mode gets set to STMMAC_CHAIN_MODE and the chain initialization routine runs; otherwise it defaults to ring mode.

Looking at the actual setup: SG2002 doesn't force chain mode through device tree or platform code, and the DTS doesn't specify it either, so it relies on the module parameter default of 0, meaning it actually runs in ring mode by default. But the user is asking whether it should use chain mode instead, which would be the better approach for DWMAC1000 without channel support.

