So the Ethernet interrupt number is **31**, connected to the PLIC (Platform-Level Interrupt Controller), which is the RISC-V interrupt controller. The interrupt is level-high triggered.

But wait, the cv180x_base.dtsi (ARM) doesn't have interrupt definitions, while the cv180x_base_riscv.dtsi (RISC-V) does. 

